{"tool_name":"proftmb","contents":["biocontainers","bioschemas","debian","biotools","oeb"],"fetched_metadata":{"biocontainers":{"name":"proftmb","identifiers":["biotools:proftmb","doi:10.1093/nar/gkl262"],"license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Per-residue prediction of bacterial transmembrane beta barrels.","home_url":"http://ppopen.informatik.tu-muenchen.de/","keywords":["Bacterial Proteins","Genome, Bacterial","Gram-Negative Bacteria","Internet","Markov Chains","Membrane Proteins","Protein Structure, Secondary","Proteomics","Sequence Analysis, Protein","User-Computer Interface","Structure prediction","Membrane and lipoproteins","Sequence Alignment","Protein Structure"],"manually_check":true,"total_pulls":0},"biotools":{"id":"proftmb","home":"http://ppopen.informatik.tu-muenchen.de/","license":"GPL-2.0","summary":"Per-residue prediction of bacterial transmembrane beta barrels.","addition_date":"2015-12-02T16:18:04Z","last_update_date":"2019-03-14T13:58:10Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool","Web application"],"version":["1.1.12"],"collections":["PredictPtotein","Rostlab tools"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:proftmb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"help@predictprotein.org","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"name":"Columbia University","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"Henry Bigelow","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Developer"]},{"name":"Irvine Cancer Center","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"RostLab","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"]},{"name":"grant R01-LM07329-01 from the National Library of Medicine","typeEntity":"Funding agency","typeRole":["Contributor"]},{"name":"Burkhard Rost","typeRole":["Contributor"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://rostlab.org/owiki/index.php/Proftmb"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Protein sequence (raw)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2974"},"format":[{"term":"FASTA-like (text)","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2200"}]}],"note":"Prediction of bacterial transmembrane beta barrels","operation":[{"term":"Protein super-secondary structure prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0268"},{"term":"Transmembrane protein prediction","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0269"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Protein report","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0896"},"format":[{"term":"Sequence feature annotation format","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_1920"}]}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"PROFtmb","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"RostLab","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkl262","metadata":{"abstract":"PROFtmb predicts transmembrane beta-barrel (TMB) proteins in Gram-negative bacteria. For each query protein, PROFtmb provides both a Z-value indicating that the protein actually contains a membrane barrel, and a four-state per-residue labeling of upward- and downward-facing strands, periplasmic hairpins and extracellular loops. While most users submit individual proteins known to contain TMBs, some groups submit entire proteomes to screen for potential TMBs. Response time is about 4 min for a 500-residue protein. PROFtmb is a profile-based Hidden Markov Model (HMM) with an architecture mirroring the structure of TMBs. The per-residue accuracy on the 8-fold cross-validated testing set is 86% while whole-protein discrimination accuracy was 70 at 60% coverage. The PROFtmb web server includes all source code, training data and whole-proteome predictions from 78 Gram-negative bacterial genomes and is available freely and without registration at http://rostlab.org/ services/proftmb. \u00a9 The Author 2006. Published by Oxford University Press. All rights reserved.","authors":[{"name":"Bigelow H."},{"name":"Rost B."}],"citationCount":45,"date":"2006-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"PROFtmb: A web server for predicting bacterial transmembrane beta barrel proteins"},"pmcid":"PMC1538807",